. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         keep if kidgeb01==2017 | kidgeb01==2018 // first child 2016 or 2017
(34,890 observations deleted)

.         keep if plh0004>0 & plh0004!=. & syear==2019 // Info on outcome
(312 observations deleted)

.         keep if (kidgeb02>0 & kidmon02>0  & kidsex01>0) | kidgeb02==-2 // Inf
> o on second child
(0 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         mvdecode plh0004 kidgeb01  kidmon01  kidsex01 kidsex02, mv(-1/-9) // 
> negatives to missing
    kidsex02: 26 missing values generated

.         mvdecode kidgeb02 kidmon02, mv(-1, -3/-7) // negatives to missing, ex
> cept -2 (no second child)

.         recode kidgeb02 (-2=0) // zero if no second child
(26 changes made to kidgeb02)

.         replace kidgeb02 = 0 if kidgeb02>2018 | (kidgeb02==2019 & kidmon02>pg
> month & syear==2019) // zero if second child born after interview
(0 real changes made)

.         replace kidsex02=0 if kidgeb02==0 // don't use second childs gender i
> f born after interview
(26 real changes made)

.         
.         gen Y = 10 - plh0004

.         label define Ylabel 0 "Completely right" 1 "9" 2 "8" 3 "7" 4 "6" 5 "5
> " ///
>                             6 "4" 7 "3" 8 "2" 9 "1" 10 "Completely left"

.         label values Y Ylabel

.         label var Y "Political Attitude on left-right spectrum" // Outcome Va
> riable

.         
.         recode kidsex01 (1=0 "Son") (2=1 "Daughter"), gen(d_daughter) // 1st 
> Child gender variable
(26 differences between kidsex01 and d_daughter)

.         label var d_daughter "1st Child Daughter"

.         
.         recode kidsex02 (.=0 "No second child") (1=1 "Son") (2=2 "Daughter"),
>  gen(second_gender) // 2nd Child gender variable
(0 differences between kidsex02 and second_gender)

.         label var second_gender "Gender of second child"

. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Description of the model:
.         * Our outcomevariable is Y = Political attitudes on a left-right spec
> trum
.         * We want to test whether having a daughter affects this outcome, and
>  we want to know whether the birth year (or time passed since birth, which ar
> e identical here) changes this effect. We also want to control for potential 
> additional children born before the outcome information was collected.
.         * We hence run a linear OLS model on Y including a dummy variable for
>  the first child being a daughter, which we interact with birth year. We also
>  include a control for the gender of the second child.
.         
. 
.         reg Y i.d_daughter##i.kidgeb01 i.second_gender, cluster(hid)
note: 0.second_gender omitted because of collinearity.

